---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "@/data/site";
import { u } from "@/data/locales";

const title = "Privacy policy — Biteperk";
const description =
  "How Biteperk collects, uses, and stores information. Plain English, Australian Privacy Act compliant.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/legal/privacy/">
  <article class="legal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[
        { label: "Home", href: u("/") },
        { label: "Legal", href: u("/legal/") },
        { label: "Privacy" },
      ]} />
      <header class="legal-head">
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated <time datetime={site.legalLastUpdated}>{site.legalLastUpdated}</time></p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Biteperk Pty Ltd (ACN {site.acn} · ABN {site.abn}) ("Biteperk", "we", "us") is an Australian company
          of {site.address.street}, {site.address.locality} {site.address.region} {site.address.postalCode}.
          We build AI voice tools for hospitality venues.
        </p>
        <p>
          This policy covers three groups of people: visitors to this website, the venues that use our
          products, and — because our products answer the phone — the people who call those venues. We handle
          personal information in line with the Australian Privacy Principles in the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>If you visit this website:</strong> when you contact us we collect the name, email, venue
          and message you provide, plus — if you arrived from a campaign link — the campaign details attached
          to that enquiry. For the website itself we use privacy-first, cookieless analytics and, only if you
          opt in, a LinkedIn marketing tag. Nothing non-essential runs until you choose <strong>Accept</strong>;
          you can change or withdraw your choice any time from <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer.
          Full details are in our <a href={u("/legal/cookies/")}>Cookie Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>If your venue uses our products:</strong> we collect your business contact details, billing
          details, and the setup information the service needs — menus, opening hours, booking rules and the
          answers you want given to common questions.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>If you call a venue that uses our products:</strong> the call is answered by the venue's AI
          assistant. Every call opens with a short announcement that you are speaking with an AI assistant and
          that the call is recorded and transcribed — before recording begins — and you can ask for a person
          or call back instead. To take your booking or order we collect the conversation (audio and
          transcript), your phone number, and the booking or order details you give: name, party size, time,
          items, special requests.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How we use it</h2>
        <p>
          We use information for one purpose: operating the service it was given to. Enquiries are used to
          reply to you; venue details are used to run and bill the products; caller information is used to
          take the booking or order and deliver it to the venue. We do not sell personal information. We do
          not share it with advertisers. We never use conversations or caller details to train AI models —
          ours or anyone else's.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Where information lives</h2>
        <p>
          Booking, order and call-summary records — and website enquiries — are stored with our cloud
          provider in Sydney, Australia. Phone calls are answered in our telephony provider's Australian
          region.
        </p>
        <p>
          Live calls are processed in real time by our voice AI platform in the United States, under written
          data-protection terms. We remain accountable under Australian privacy law for how our overseas
          providers handle that information — we choose independently security-certified platforms, and we do
          not treat overseas processing as someone else's problem. The country involved is the United States.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Call recordings and transcripts are automatically and permanently deleted after 30 days (venues may
          select up to 90). Booking and order records are kept while the venue remains a client, because they
          are the venue's business records. Website enquiries are kept only as long as needed to deal with
          them. Any caller can ask for their details, or a specific recording, to be deleted sooner.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Automated decisions</h2>
        <p>
          Our products are automated: an AI assistant answers the call, offers available booking times based
          on rules the venue sets, and records the booking or order. Callers are always told they are speaking
          with an AI and can ask for a person instead, and every booking and order is delivered to venue staff,
          who can review and correct it. We do not use automation to profile callers, and the assistant creates
          no voiceprints and performs no biometric identification.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask what information we hold about you, and ask for it to be accessed, corrected or deleted —
          whether you are a client, a website visitor, or someone who called a venue we serve. Email
          <a href={site.email.href}>{site.email.display}</a> and we'll respond within 30 days — usually much
          sooner.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If you think we've mishandled your information, tell us first at
          <a href={site.email.href}>{site.email.display}</a> — we'll acknowledge your complaint within 5
          business days and respond properly within 20. If you're not satisfied with our response, you can
          complain to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at
          <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use industry-standard practices: encrypted transit, encrypted storage, least-privilege access
          with multi-factor authentication, and independently certified platforms. Short retention is part of
          security too — recordings that no longer exist can't be stolen. No system is perfect; if you spot a
          problem, please email us before posting it publicly so we can fix it quickly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          This site may link to sites we don't run. Their privacy practices are their own — check their
          policies before giving them information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Updates</h2>
        <p>
          We'll update this policy as the business changes. Material changes will be noted at the top with a
          new "last updated" date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Privacy questions: <a href={site.email.href}>{site.email.display}</a> or call
          <a href={site.phone.href}>{site.phone.display}</a> ({site.hours.display}).
          Biteperk Pty Ltd · ABN {site.abn} · {site.address.street}, {site.address.locality}
          {site.address.region} {site.address.postalCode}.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: clamp(120px, 14vw, 180px) 0 var(--space-section);
    background: var(--ink-0);
  }
  .legal .wrap { max-width: 720px; }
  .legal-head { margin-top: 32px; }
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    color: var(--white);
  }
  .legal-updated {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--mist);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .legal section { margin-top: 48px; }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2vw, 24px);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--white);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .legal p {
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .legal a {
    color: var(--gold);
    /* Underline so in-prose links don't rely on colour alone (WCAG 1.4.1). */
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .legal a:hover { text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
</style>
